    "id": 85,
    "title": "The site's icon in every tab",
    "why": "Jason, 2026-11-17: \"can you check why our ico is not working on traversence when it is working on staging?\" Only the home page and the classic directory linked an icon (the home page by a relative path that broke on deeper routes); every other page fell back to /favicon.ico, which didn't exist, so the tab showed a blank globe. Now a real /favicon.ico sits at the web root (the T mark at 16, 32, 48 and 64 px), a 180 px home-screen icon (the North Star compass on the bar's brown), and one helper (app/ui/favicon.php) prints the icon lines with root-absolute paths in every shared head: the page shell (so the whole admin), tv_nav_head, the chamber builder, the order manifest, the home page and the classic directory. trvgo.us pages use Traversence's icon from traversence.com; a storefront shows the business's own logo when it has one.",
